Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Honor an explicit large-address-aware disable override.

This is an opt-in compatibility workaround, not an upstream Wine backport.
CrossOver's force_laa() can force large-address awareness on, but an environment
value of 0 currently cannot override IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE in the PE
header. Honor the exact WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=0 value for that case too.
Unset, 1, and every other value retain the existing behavior.

A 32-bit FreeArc LargestMemoryBlock probe computes (low + high) / 2 with
size_t, initially 0 and UINT_MAX. If its first 0x7fffffff-byte reservation
succeeds, the next sum wraps. It eventually reaches low=1/high=0 and loops
forever probing zero bytes. An explicit 2 GiB automatic allocation search range prevents
that initial reservation while preserving normal LAA behavior by default.
Native 64-bit processes retain their existing address-space behavior.

Primary source for the probe's arithmetic:
https://github.com/phyxolog/FreeArc/blob/721118f7e3e506cfde32f8febeddf274b3a83d75/Environment.cpp#L222-L230

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5106,6 +5106,12 @@
 void virtual_set_large_address_space(void)
 {
     BOOL large_address_space_active = ((main_image_info.ImageCharacteristics & IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE) || force_laa());
+    const char *large_address_space_override = getenv( "WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE" );
+
+    /* Opt-in 2 GiB automatic allocation range, including PE LAA images, for
+     * 32-bit FreeArc probes whose midpoint sum overflows above the signed boundary. */
+    if (large_address_space_override && !strcmp( large_address_space_override, "0" ))
+        large_address_space_active = FALSE;
     if (is_win64)
     {
         if (!is_wow64())
